# G9POS — UI / UX Rules

## The One Rule
The shop owner must be able to complete a sale in under 10 seconds without reading anything.

## Primary User
A non-technical shop owner operating alone. She is serving customers and handling cash simultaneously. She cannot afford to be confused by the app for even 5 seconds. Design for her first, always.

## Design Tokens — Always Use These

```dart
// Colors — never hardcode hex inline
AppColors.primary          // #1B4FFF — main actions
AppColors.success          // #16A34A — complete, in stock
AppColors.warning          // #F59E0B — low stock, stale sync
AppColors.error            // #DC2626 — void, delete, negative stock
AppColors.textPrimary      // #111111
AppColors.textSecondary    // #666666
AppColors.surface          // #FFFFFF
AppColors.background       // #F5F5F5

// Spacing — always AppSpacing.*
AppSpacing.xs   // 4px
AppSpacing.sm   // 8px
AppSpacing.md   // 16px
AppSpacing.lg   // 24px
AppSpacing.xl   // 32px

// Text — always AppTextStyles.*
AppTextStyles.saleTotal      // 40px, w800 — checkout total
AppTextStyles.cartItemName   // 16px, w600
AppTextStyles.body           // 15px, w400
AppTextStyles.caption        // 12px, w400
AppTextStyles.buttonPrimary  // 17px, w700, white
```

## Touch Targets — No Exceptions
Minimum tap target: **48×48px**. Use padding to enforce this on small icons.
```dart
// ✅ Correct
IconButton(
  iconSize: 24,
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(AppSpacing.md), // total = 56px
  onPressed: onPressed,
  icon: Icon(Icons.remove),
)
// ❌ Wrong
GestureDetector(onTap: onTap, child: Icon(Icons.remove, size: 16))
```

Key action buttons (Complete Sale, Confirm Void, Save): minimum height 56px.

## Navigation — Bottom Bar Only
```dart
// 4 tabs, always visible
// [🛒 POS] [📦 Products] [📊 Reports] [⚙️ Settings]
```
No drawer. No hamburger menu. No nested navigation more than 1 level deep.

## Layout — Tablet vs Phone
```dart
// Breakpoint: 600px
LayoutBuilder(builder: (context, constraints) {
  if (constraints.maxWidth >= 600) {
    return TabletLayout(); // split: products left 60%, cart right 40%
  }
  return PhoneLayout(); // product grid full width, cart as bottom sheet
})
```

## POS Sale Screen Rules
- Total is always visible — never below the fold
- "COMPLETE SALE" button: full width of cart panel, 64px tall, `AppColors.primary`
- Cart item row: name left, (− N +) center, price right
- Search bar always visible at top — not hidden behind a tap
- No settings, reports, or unrelated items on this screen

## Sync Status Indicator
Shown in app header on every screen — never blocking:
```
🟢 = synced < 2h ago (icon only)
🟡 = 2–4h ago (icon only)
🟠 = 4–24h ago (icon + time text)
🔴 = >24h ago (icon + time text, tappable → sync screen)
```

## Offline Banner
```dart
// Slim banner below header when no connectivity — amber, 36px tall
// "⚡ Offline — sales are saving locally"
// Disappears automatically when connectivity returns
// Never blocks any action
```

## Error Messages
```dart
// ✅ Correct — plain language, inline under field
Text('Could not save product. Try again.', style: AppTextStyles.caption.copyWith(color: AppColors.error))

// ❌ Wrong — never SnackBar for errors
ScaffoldMessenger.of(context).showSnackBar(SnackBar(content: Text(e.toString())));

// ❌ Wrong — never expose raw exceptions
Text(exception.toString())
```

## Confirmation Dialogs
Required for: void sale, delete product, sign out, mark order received.
Not required for: add to cart, remove from cart, complete sale, save product.

Dialog rules:
- Maximum 2 buttons
- Destructive action: right side, `AppColors.error`
- Cancel: left side, grey
- Title: plain language ("Cancel this sale?")
- Body: honest — never promise what cannot be guaranteed

**Void confirmation body (§11.2 — Design 1):**
```
"If the shop still allows cancelling this sale today, stock will be put back. 
If not, the sale will stay completed."
```
Never say "This cannot be undone." Never promise stock will definitely be returned.

## Currency Formatting
```dart
// Always use CurrencyFormatter — never format inline
CurrencyFormatter.format(13000)    // → "13,000 MMK"
CurrencyFormatter.formatCompact(13000) // → "13,000"

// ❌ Wrong
Text('${amount} MMK')
```

## Date / Timezone
```dart
// Always ShopDateUtils — never DateTime.now() in business logic
ShopDateUtils.nowInShop()
ShopDateUtils.isSameShopDay(a, b)
```

## Loading States
- First app launch: full-screen spinner (only this case)
- Lists and grids: shimmer skeleton matching real item shape
- Individual actions: inline spinner
- Never block the entire UI for a background operation

## What Cursor Must Never Do in UI Code
- ❌ `SnackBar` for errors
- ❌ `showDialog` for non-destructive feedback
- ❌ Hardcode any color, font size, or spacing value
- ❌ Show raw exception or stack trace to user
- ❌ Block a sale action with a loading spinner
- ❌ Use red for anything except destructive actions and errors
- ❌ Use a drawer or hamburger menu
- ❌ Use a bottom sheet for the main cart on tablet
- ❌ Require more than 3 taps for any common daily action
- ❌ Import `package:drift` directly in a widget or screen file
